  "id": "ex-05-adjektivdeklination-a2",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. After der/die/das (the article already shows gender+case), the adjective just adds -e or -en — \"schwache\" endings. After ein/eine/ein (the article is silent in maskulin Nominativ and neutral Nominativ/Akkusativ), the adjective has to show it instead — \"gemischte\" endings: ein GUTER Mann, ein GUTES Kind. Everywhere else, ein and der behave the same. Blocks: A Basistraining (the two tables) → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/05-adjektivdeklination-a2",
  "level": "A2",
  "summary": null,
  "title": "Adjektivendungen nach der/ein — A2",
  "topic": "Adjektivdeklination (schwach, gemischt, stark)"
